linux-hardware-monitor (0.2.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Packages for Ubuntu 22.04 and Ubuntu 24.04: the program now builds with
    Qt 6.2 and newer (before: 6.5).
  * The package depends on qml6-module-qtqml-workerscript, which the window
    needs and which the Controls package of Ubuntu 24.04 does not pull in.
  * The packages know the commit they were built from: --version and the About
    page show the build.
  * Builds without warnings on the newest toolchains (Fedora 44, Arch Linux:
    Qt 6.11 / 6.12, GCC 16). Proxy models use the filter-change calls of
    Qt 6.9 where they exist.
  * --dump-json reports an error when it cannot write its output.
  * A test now starts the application for every page and fails on a QML
    error; the quit-signal test can no longer signal its whole process group.

 -- Zbara <zbara.dev@gmail.com>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 20:59:52 +0200

linux-hardware-monitor (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New setting for the CPU temperature: the package sensor (default), the
    hottest core or the average of the cores. The tiles say which reading
    they show and the tray follows the choice.
  * New theme setting: follow the desktop, dark or light. The choice of earlier
    versions is kept.
  * Overheat notifications are grouped, one per device instead of one for each
    of the processor's core sensors.
  * About page: author and website, the build (commit), Qt version, system and
    graphics backend. --version prints the build, Qt and license as well.
  * The settings are a centred column and long hints wrap instead of being cut.
  * The README has its License and Author sections.

 -- Zbara <zbara.dev@gmail.com>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:41:08 +0200

linux-hardware-monitor (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First public release.
  * Performance, Processes, Services, Startup apps, Sensors and Overview pages
    with CPU, memory, disk, network, GPU and battery graphs.
  * Sensor history with per-sensor statistics and CSV export.
  * Disk health (SMART through udisks2), temperature unit setting, optional
    notifications for overheating, thermal throttling and a stopped fan.
  * Simulation mode, JSON dump of all sensors for scripts and headless machines.
  * Translations: English, Russian, Ukrainian, German, Spanish.

 -- Zbara <zbara.dev@gmail.com>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0200
